{"left":{"id":"db1d24a7-26ea-44b7-870c-246055703b65","word":"left","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"remaining","word":"deixado"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"remaining","word":"sobrar"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"remaining","word":"restar"}],"pos":"verb","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"There's not much food left.","bold_text_offsets":[[22,26]],"type":"example","id":"ab77dccb-29a5-4cbd-a07e-4d89fc202cad"},{"text":"Afore we got to the shanty Colonel Applegate stuck his head out of the door. His temper had been getting raggeder all the time, and the sousing he got when he fell overboard had just about ripped what was left of it to ravellings.","ref":"1913, Joseph C[rosby] Lincoln, chapter VIII, in Mr. Pratt’s Patients, New York, N.Y.; London: D[aniel] Appleton and Company, →OCLC:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[205,209]],"id":"5ef11507-e13e-4de3-82ed-ce7c82f097d0"},{"text":"Shepard: What's wrong with your assistant?\nDr. Warren: Manuel has a brilliant mind, but he's always been a bit... unstable. Genius and madness are two sides of the same coin.\nDr. Manuel: Is it madness to see the future? To see the destruction rushing towards us? To understand there is no escape? No hope? No, I am not mad. I'm the only sane one left!\nDr. Warren: I gave him an extra dose of his meds after the attack.","ref":"2008, BioWare, Mass Effect (Science Fiction), Redwood City: Electronic Arts, →ISBN, →OCLC, PC, scene: Eden Prime:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[346,350]],"id":"dfd8a1db-8ad3-42d4-8093-9772529f831a"}],"links":[["leave","leave#English"]],"categories":["English terms with quotations","English terms with usage examples"],"glosses":["simple past and past participle of leave (“depart, separate from; (cause or allow to) remain”)."],"tags":["form-of","participle","past"],"form_of":[{"word":"leave","extra":"(“depart, separate from; (cause or allow to) remain”)"}],"id":"0e4e877d-5230-4c0a-94cc-0fc1abe9bca3"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"left-handed":{"id":"9fc5147f-6f79-4741-8d1d-788f399fa384","word":"left-handed","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"preferring the left hand over the right","word":"canhoto"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"preferring the left hand over the right","word":"sestro"}],"pos":"adj","tags":null,"senses":[{"links":[["left","left"],["hand","hand#Noun"],["preference","preference"],["skillfully","skillfully"],["right","right"]],"glosses":["Using one's left hand in preference to, or more skillfully than, one's right."],"tags":["not-comparable"],"id":"a4dcd29d-1b9e-44b3-a2e5-c799d15ef9c9"},{"links":[["worn","wear#Verb"],["used","use#Verb"]],"glosses":["Intended to be worn on, or used by, the left hand."],"tags":["not-comparable"],"id":"f6135b98-2248-4b42-92a7-24d56744d4aa"},{"links":[["Turning","turn#Verb"],["spiraling","spiral#Verb"],["anticlockwise","anticlockwise"]],"glosses":["Turning or spiraling from right to left; anticlockwise."],"tags":["not-comparable"],"id":"076ac3b0-0814-4234-8de9-5e7ee36fc154"},{"links":[["Awkward","awkward"],["maladroit","maladroit"]],"glosses":["Awkward or maladroit."],"tags":["not-comparable"],"id":"bcc2208f-af31-46f5-9ce5-8084cc05c2ee"},{"examples":[{"text":"The commendations of this people are not always […]left-handed and detractive.","ref":"1824, Walter Savage Landor, “Aeschines and Phocion”, in Imaginary Conversations of Literary Men and Statesmen, volume I, London: […] Taylor and Hessey, […], →OCLC:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[51,62]],"id":"40dda9c2-d503-4cd7-bd9d-5926bb041e8f"}],"glosses":["Insincere or malicious."],"categories":["English terms with quotations"],"tags":["not-comparable"],"id":"d7cf8914-63a2-48ed-a8bb-9e9298d6d861"},{"examples":[{"text":"On the other hand, nearly all magic tends in time to the left-handed path; as being a devious means of attaining desires unobtainable by 